cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use DART in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "DART: Diffusion-Augmented Reliable Transformer Serving"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Aydiner"
    given-names: "Tugrap"
repository-code: "https://github.com/tugrapaydiner/dart"
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.3.0
keywords:
  - speculative decoding
  - diffusion language models
  - KV-cache compression
  - LLM inference
  - exact verification
abstract: >-
  DART is a single-sequence LLM inference engine with diffusion, multi-token,
  n-gram, compressed-KV and sparse-KV draft lanes. A target model verifies
  token proposals. Complete reference comparisons assess numerical agreement
  for each model, device, precision and attention backend. Canvas
  reconciliation repairs the unverified suffix after rejection. Local
  Supra-50M presets, bounded teacher traces and compact training support
  reproducible decoding experiments.
